    {
      "heading": "Uno, un, una",
      "body": "When you count, say *uno*. Before a masculine noun it shortens to *un*: *un libro*. Before a feminine noun it's *una*: *una mesa*. The same happens at the end of bigger numbers later (*veintiún años*)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The verb tener (to have)",
      "body": "*Tener* means \"to have\". It is irregular — memorise it now, you'll use it constantly.",
      "table": {
        "head": [
          "Pronoun",
