    {
      "heading": "Saying your age",
      "body": "Spanish uses *tener* for age — you literally \"have\" years: *Tengo veinte años* (I'm twenty). Never use *ser* for age.\n\nTo ask: *¿Cuántos años tienes?* (How old are you? — informal) or *¿Cuántos años tiene usted?* (formal). *¿Cuántos?* means \"how many?\"\n\nA useful related phrase: *Tengo dos hermanos* (I have two siblings) — *hermano* means brother, *hermana* sister."
    }
  ],
